{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Like the waters of Noah.</b> The flood that was in the days of Noah." "<b>This.</b> The meaning: this decree that I decreed, and the consolation that I spoke." "And just as I swore that no flood like the waters of Noah would again pass over the earth — and this is the verse: \"and I will never again strike every living thing\" (Genesis 8:21)." "And the meaning of <b>the rebuke upon you</b> — because He compared her to an abandoned woman."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 54, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:30.662857431Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}